
Implement the smallest safe integration of BASE
and JVM_SYSTEM_PROPERTIES configuration sources.

The existing TestNG lifecycle adapter already
loads XML parameters at SUITE, TEST, CLASS
and INVOCATION scopes.

The missing sources are BASE and
JVM_SYSTEM_PROPERTIES.

Requirements:

1. Reuse the existing classpath properties
   source and configuration file layer loader.

2. Load the existing test.config.properties
   into the ROOT configuration context as BASE.

3. Reuse the existing JVM system property
   layer loader.

4. Load JVM system properties into ROOT using
   the JVM_SYSTEM_PROPERTIES source type.

5. Preserve the established source priority:
   BASE < ENVIRONMENT < FRAMEWORK_PARAMETERS
   < PROGRAMMATIC < JVM_SYSTEM_PROPERTIES
   < EXPLICIT_OVERRIDE.

6. Ensure ROOT layers are initialized before
   child contexts resolve configuration.

7. Initialize each layer only once per
   owned ROOT context.

8. Preserve thread safety and atomic visibility
   during initialization.

9. Do not modify externally owned ROOT contexts
   without explicit authorization.

10. Preserve existing environment selection
    and XML parameter inheritance.

11. Do not change the configuration resolver.

12. Do not modify the existing properties manager.

13. Do not migrate existing listeners yet.

14. Do not introduce global mutable state,
    another coordinator or another registry.

Add focused integration tests verifying:

- BASE properties are loaded into ROOT.
- JVM system properties are available.
- JVM values override XML and PROGRAMMATIC
  values for the same key.
- EXPLICIT_OVERRIDE remains the highest priority.
- Child contexts inherit ROOT configuration.
- Parallel invocations remain isolated.
- No duplicate layers are created.
- Repeated executions use independent ROOTs.
- Configuration layers are removed during cleanup.

Use explicit test-defined expected values,
not the existing properties manager as the
correctness oracle.

Run the focused tests, the complete TestNG
module and the Maven reactor build.

Report exact results and any compatibility
issues discovered.

Keep changes minimal and focused.










